$ distinct singular values.\n- **II.** The matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$ has one negative singular value.\n- **III.** Any $5\\times 3$ matrix $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values." :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $3\\times 3$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{3\\times 2}\\times {A}_{2\\times 3}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{3\\times 3}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values.\n\n- Statement II is false. All singular values of any matrix are non-negative. So, $A$ can't have a negative singular value.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ is a $5\\times 3$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $3\\times 5$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $3\\times 3$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{3\\times 5}\\times {A}_{5\\times 3}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{3\\times 3}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416485 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4129371-905f-54bf-ae87-c438b2fd43aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454184} {:answer/id #uuid "77bf2baa-cff5-52ce-8b41-e36aedb6e4a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454185}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454185} :answer-field/id #uuid "861de6d8-648e-5127-85e8-5f06c2f6e1e5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454842} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4731f9ee-31e7-5b9b-a569-ce496f29e4a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #e